omx-dsp (0.30.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.30.0: changelog line for the checks
  * packaging: omx-contract is required from 3.9.0 and before 4
  * ci: build on omx-contract 3.9.0; the wave branch of omx-contract is gone
  * copy-check's clean-consumer arm reads a tree
  * Checks: reading no file is red, and SPDX is the shared check's
  * test/contract: a use of no declared item is refused in omx-contract's new
    words
  * ci: a dedupe/all run reads omx-contract's dedupe/all in the contract and
    fuzz jobs
  * release: omx-dsp 0.30.0, on omx-contract 3.9.0
  * ci: a pull request into dedupe/all builds on omx-contract's dedupe/all
  * packaging: the Debian .docs and .install lists carry the licence lines
  * comp: DETECTOR_TOPOLOGY carries its labels, the one place both plugins
    read
  * dynamics: a program release inside the feedback loop recovers one way
  * glue: detectorTopology takes comp's DETECTOR_TOPOLOGY, no copy
  * fastmath: every sample of a libmvec loop through the vector call,
    whatever the block
  * fastmath: the block size through the libmvec loops, and no libm call in
    them
  * glue: detectorTopology, appended last, default feedforward
  * dynamics: the feedback loop's attack never passes the held input's
    equilibrium
  * gaincomp: one floor for every ABOVE reduction, omx_gaincomp_floor
  * delay: 1/32 divisions; with no host tempo a synced delay keeps its time
  * packaging: every package installs its licence and the short README
  * packaging: no markdown in the packages; their descriptions name
    openmixer.org

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 02:45:58 +0000
